			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0b122070-9044-56ac-b176-3379338fe6fc")
	)
	(text "U2: JTAG buffer. R2 holds /OE HIGH, so the ESP32 is OFF the JTAG bus through its own\nboot and whenever firmware has not claimed it -- the Pt's USB/FT2232H path wins by default\n(README 4.2). R3 parks ESP_TDO while the buffer is off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 500 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "77ef575a-c154-59dc-933e-2c7e6802aefc")
	)
	(text "JTAG STRAPS -- populate R10-R13 for Pt V2 rev A (as built), OR R14-R17 for rev B.\nNEVER BOTH: that shorts two JTAG lines together.  Rev B moves JTAG to the Au V2 order."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 465 228 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21450465-7f92-5a6f-998d-6276b1664dfd")
	)
	(text "Q1/Q2 pull PROGRAM_B / Reset low only when the ESP32 drives the gate high.\nR4/R5 keep them OFF while GPIOs float at boot -- a bitstream is never lost to a reset glitch.\nR6: DONE is read-only; 1k limits current if the GPIO is ever misconfigured as output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 465 290 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f6f0b2f5-5cfd-51d1-bbeb-f0feffd90043")
	)
	(text "ESP32 <-> fabric SPI on J3 29-36 (README 3b). SCK/MOSI/MISO/CS/IO2/IO3 on the\nS3's IO_MUX FSPI pins, so quad SPI at 80 MHz is available without the GPIO matrix.\nBanks 14 and 34 are 3.3 V (bank 13 is the only 2.5 V bank) -- confirm VCCO before first use."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 335 244 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0d4e3b63-0dd6-589e-b284-3ec3ff32f40d")
	)
	(text "J7 microSD, 1.42 mm tall -- TOP face only (SD_BITSTREAM_LIBRARY 3).\n10k pull-ups on CMD/DAT0-3 per the SD spec. Detect switch 9-10 -> SD_CD_N."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 335 300 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "03727ff4-43b6-51ae-9edb-728050aa0d57")
	)
	(text "Pad field for first flash / recovery -- place at the enclosure's open face.\nUSB_DP/DN = GPIO20/19 (native USB-Serial-JTAG). ESP_BOOT = GPIO0: hold low + pulse EN.\nTP1-TP8 are bare copper: no part, not in the BOM or CPL."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 520 320 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc9d4a6d-e56f-539e-81f3-58b6ecd653fc")
	)
	(text "LauEsp32Config_Pt_Stack -- ESP32 wireless programmer, Pt V2 element card.\nGENERATED by gen_schematic.py -- edit the script, not this sheet. Design notes: SCHEMATIC.md.\nEvery assembled part carries an LCSC code; check_jlc_parts.py verifies code, MPN and stock."
